{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions","id":589983,"title":"[Dark Eras] Great Cults of Major Religions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-14T00:16:04-07:00","id":589983,"title":"[Dark Eras] Great Cults of Major Religions","content":"<i><b>To the Strongest</b></i> historical <b>Mage</b> Chapter in <b>Dark Eras</b> gives us next &quot;faction&quot; tier beside the Paths and (quasi-Orders of ) Darshanas - they are so called Great Cults that describe Awakened cosmology in terms of nations major religions the particants adhere to, because before the era of common globalisation ( from XIX century onward ) world of mages were fratureted to what Mysteries you belive in. After creation of Orders those views started to become unified, but Great Cults still been the root of most theories the new Awakaned dwell to.<br /> <br /> When waching the video below about spread of 5 modern major religons of our world, I thought that it would be very interesting and usefull to have Great Cults of those and answer big qustion - <b>How Buddist, Chrisitan, Hindu, Islam and Jew, mages loon on the cosmology of <i>Mage</i> game?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/map-shows-how-religion-spread-around-the-world-2015-6#ooid=F5aHR4dTob1y4-cHP5qNzXITGcq1vPVW\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.insider.com/5592b198ecad043944169e90?width=1200&amp;format=jpeg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/map-shows-how-religion-spread-around-the-world-2015-6#ooid=F5aHR4dTob1y4-cHP5qNzXITGcq1vPVW\" target=\"_blank\"> This animated map shows how religion spread across the world </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/map-shows-how-religion-spread-around-the-world-2015-6#ooid=F5aHR4dTob1y4-cHP5qNzXITGcq1vPVW\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.businessinsider.com/map-shows-how-religion-spread-around-the-world-2015-6#ooid=F5aHR4dTob1y4-cHP5qNzXITGcq1vPVW </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> VIDEO: 5,000 years of religious history in two minutes. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><b>To the Strongest</b></i> gives us the those Cults:<ul><li><b>Arcadian Mysteries</b> ( called also<i> Pelasgians</i> ) based on myths of Ancient Greece.</li> <li><b>Karpani </b>( called also Magi ) based on Zoroastrian charge of Ancient Persia.</li> <li><b>Mantra Sadhaki</b> are Hindu mages rooting their views in Naga Kingdom.</li> <li><b>Weret-Hekau</b> are Egyptian priests of Five-Fold Souls.</li> </ul>As we have Hindu Cult, how do you see the other four major religions view Awakened cosmology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-14-2015, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T02:54:13-07:00","id":590070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> because before the era of common globalisation ( from XIX century onward ) world of mages were fratureted to what Mysteries you belive in. </div> </div> </div>That's not the first time. The Great Cults seem to exist where you have fairly homogenous cultures (plus India, but I'll ignore that for the moment). To The Strongest represents the beginning of an era where there's a great deal of pluralism, and Magi can easily compare and draw on multiple traditions. That's something which fluctuates over history. I mean, much of Europe becomes totally dominated by Christianity, but the areas of the Muslim empire are fairly pluralistic for a much longer period.<br /> <br /> I mean, how does a Jewish great cult work when by the nature of being a minority in a larger population they're going to be regularly interacting with non-Jewish magi (and visa versa to an extent)?<br /> <br /> (India is a bit of an outlier because at the period of To The Strongest it's already a very pluralistic place. I mean, Hinduism is kinda a label slapped on a very eclectic mixture of beliefs and religions. There's a reason it began life as a geographical term.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T03:20:00-07:00","id":590074,"title":"","content":"I have other observation on the topic - that in their core Jew, Christian and Islam would still be one <i><b>Monotheistic Great Cult</b></i>. All three religions would loosely interpret Supernal Realms in the same way ( Arcadia and Primal Wild as Garden of Eden, Stygia as Purgatory/Gehenna, Pandemonium as Hell, Aether as Heaven ) and even their magical practice will come one from another. The only real dirffence is that Jews would have much more Silver Ladder overtones ( and divine Hierarchy ), Christian would be more entwined with Guardians Heiromagus idea ( and Church's conspiracies ) and Islam will have a more Adamantine Arrow outlook ( with their tendency to Jihad ). But it would be only slight bias. Over all, they will be using the same Symbols and very similar myths in their magic. Compared to other, they will be just three different flavors on the same subjects, <b>not</b> totally different answers.<br /> <br /> But Buddists would be very interesting, as their philosophy is almost radically different from other four major religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-14-2015, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T04:21:50-07:00","id":590135,"title":"","content":"I think a Christian-Islamic sect would overlook that they exist in quite different cultures. The Great cults aren't just marked by different mythos, but by different ways of organisation.<br /> Also, I think It's important I think to remember that the various great cults are not just their respective religions plus magic. The Arcadians are highly ambivelant towards their Gods, the zoroastrian magi are actually pretty disreputable.<br /> <br /> I kinda wonder if a Christian great cult wouldn't be something like Catharism or Gnosticism. Recognisably Christian but still quite different from the mainstream.<br /> <br /> Thinking about Europe specifically, I've kinda wondered about retooling the Messianic Singers from Dark Ages Mage. Despite being an Ascension group, I think they kinda fit what I'm talking about pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:38:50-07:00","id":590500,"title":"","content":"Christian Gnosticism sounds pretty much exactly like what I'd expect from faithful Christians trying to make sense of the world after awakening.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Gnosticism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Gnosticism\" target=\"_blank\"> Gnosticism - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Gnosticism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Gnosticism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T17:11:08-07:00","id":590606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590074#post590074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have other observation on the topic - that in their core Jew, Christian and Islam would still be one <i><b>Monotheistic Great Cult</b></i>. All three religions would loosely interpret Supernal Realms in the same way ( Arcadia and Primal Wild as Garden of Eden, Stygia as Purgatory/Gehenna, Pandemonium as Hell, Aether as Heaven ) and even their magical practice will come one from another. The only real dirffence is that Jews would have much more Silver Ladder overtones ( and divine Hierarchy ), Christian would be more entwined with Guardians Heiromagus idea ( and Church's conspiracies ) and Islam will have a more Adamantine Arrow outlook ( with their tendency to Jihad ). But it would be only slight bias. Over all, they will be using the same Symbols and very similar myths in their magic. Compared to other, they will be just three different flavors on the same subjects, <b>not</b> totally different answers.<br /> <br /> But Buddists would be very interesting, as their philosophy is almost radically different from other four major religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... really don't know much about Judaism.<br /> <br /> The Jewish conception of Heaven is incredibly different from the Christian or Islamic concept to the point where using the same word is entirely misleading. Jews don't believe in Hell or &quot;the Devil&quot; (in Jewish mythos ha'satan is a title/job description for an angel and angels can't fall because they lack free will). Gehenna as a form of Purgatory isn't really modern mainstream thought, though it does have some theological grounding.<br /> <br /> I also don't see how Judaism would have Silver Ladder overtones at all except amongst the most ultra of ultra-Orthodox and the Hassidim. Most Jews tend to towards secularism, and even those that don't tend to be anti-authoritarian and socially liberal. There's a reason that Jews go solidly for Democrats in the US and, while Bibi's Likud is right-wing it's still relatively centrist in a liberal democracy. Jews also tend heavily towards higher education in arts and sciences and the religion itself supports the idea that it is through <i>human</i> deeds that things change and the world is made better (or: as Below, so Above), pointing to a more Libertine mindset if anything.<br /> <br /> If anything it's the Catholics that would tend more towards the Silver Ladder based purely on their religion as they have a very clearly defined temporal hierarchy.<br /> <br /> <br /> All that being said: I think it's a tenuous connection at best to link a Sleeper's religion to what Order they choose after Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:20:38-07:00","id":590890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590606#post590606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You... really don't know much about Judaism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying I'm. I'm only Christian raised nerd on Mage forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590606#post590606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jewish conception of Heaven is incredibly different from the Christian or Islamic concept to the point where using the same word is entirely misleading. Jews don't believe in Hell or &quot;the Devil&quot; (in Jewish mythos ha'satan is a title/job description for an angel and angels can't fall because they lack free will). Gehenna as a form of Purgatory isn't really modern mainstream thought, though it does have some theological grounding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was basing most of it from the those rare events I made contact with Jew culture - clearly, not enought. Also, I was basing this interpretation on Awakaned <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabbalah\" target=\"_blank\">Kaballah</a> from <b>Magical Traditions</b>. How much it is relevant to the Judaism on large I still do not know. But if Christian Great Cult would be Gnostic Christianity, so I assume Jews would use here Kaballah, yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590606#post590606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't see how Judaism would have Silver Ladder overtones at all except amongst the most ultra of ultra-Orthodox and the Hassidim. Most Jews tend to towards secularism, and even those that don't tend to be anti-authoritarian and socially liberal. There's a reason that Jews go solidly for Democrats in the US and, while Bibi's Likud is right-wing it's still relatively centrist in a liberal democracy. Jews also tend heavily towards higher education in arts and sciences and the religion itself supports the idea that it is through <i>human</i> deeds that things change and the world is made better (or: as Below, so Above), pointing to a more Libertine mindset if anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were only broad strokes to point that Monoteistic Cult would be devided in to three flavors, not proper Great Cults itself. But if you feel that Judaism would made totally diffrent Cult from Christian-Islam one, maybe point in what places? Compare them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:46:17-07:00","id":590919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590890#post590890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying I'm. I'm only Christian raised nerd on Mage forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine, I just get a little tired of the conflation of Jewish and Christian thought (99% of the time you're going to label something &quot;Judeo-Christian&quot; it'd be more accurate to just say &quot;Christian&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was basing most of it from the those rare events I made contact with Jew culture - clearly, not enought. Also, I was basing this interpretation on Awakaned <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabbalah\" target=\"_blank\">Kaballah</a> from <b>Magical Traditions</b>. How much it is relevant to the Judaism on large I still do not know. But if Christian Great Cult would be Gnostic Christianity, so I assume Jews would use here Kaballah, yes? </div> </div> </div>The use of Kabbalah would depend on the Jew. The Conservative and Reform movements have excised Kabbalistic practices. But even for those that do use Kabbalah, it's not really an occult book or a book on how to engage in mystic practice, it's a theology book that contains some mysticism. It's more a way to decipher the Torah than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were only broad strokes to point that Monoteistic Cult would be devided in to three flavors, not proper Great Cults itself. But if you feel that Judaism would made totally diffrent Cult from Christian-Islam one, maybe point in what places? Compare them. </div> </div> </div>I think that while there might be a single Jewish Awakened Cult (there's not that many Jews and the major division between Jews is strictness of practice not really core doctrinal interpretation) I'd be surprised if there weren't <i>at least</i> a Catholic Cult, an Orthodox Christian Cult, and (many) Protestant Cult(s). There'd also likely be two, or more, Islamic Cults (shia/suuni and possibly the different Asians).<br /> <br /> I also imagine that any Jewish Great Cult would only be a Great Cult due to a combination of tradition, real world bleed-over, and influence of its members <i>or</i> Jews would have to have a way higher percentage of Awakenings than pretty much any other group. 2 tenths of a percent of the world population doesn't leave for a lot of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-22-2018, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:17:00-07:00","id":590958,"title":"","content":"Sorry for flinging with bad stereotypes on Jewish faith. Forgive me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590919#post590919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that while there might be a single Jewish Awakened Cult (there's not that many Jews and the major division between Jews is strictness of practice not really core doctrinal interpretation) I'd be surprised if there weren't <i>at least</i> a Catholic Cult, an Orthodox Christian Cult, and (many) Protestant Cult(s). There'd also likely be two, or more, Islamic Cults (shia/suuni and possibly the different Asians).</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I would oposed - Great Cults are based on idea that you made a large enough and diverse sect in to general strokes of Awakened reinterpretation. Christian would still be one Cult, becuase diffrences like existance of Trinity or Holiness of Virigin Mary is not enough to break this, the essence of it's mytholodgy.<br /> <br /> Look on original <b>Mantra Sadhaki</b> Great Cult - they are thousands of Hindu religions and worships, connected by major mythology roots and belive in Naga Kingdom. The same can be said about Christian Cult - they belive in Jesus as Hieromagus figure and Ain Soph God that rules universe. Great Cults are &quot;Great&quot; becuase they paint Awakaned mythos with &quot;big brushes&quot;. Still, mages from them can easily fight with one another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=590919#post590919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also imagine that any Jewish Great Cult would only be a Great Cult due to a combination of tradition, real world bleed-over, and influence of its members <i>or</i> Jews would have to have a way higher percentage of Awakenings than pretty much any other group. 2 tenths of the world population doesn't leave for a lot of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really like to see what you can made for Jewish Cult. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T09:01:52-07:00","id":591386,"title":"","content":"A Cult seems to me like what happens post-Fall to a society of Awakened developing without broad contact with mages from other cultures. Each of the cults is a sort of proto-Diamond, more reminiscent of the host culture because they don't have any other cultures with which to compare notes to see which symbols and themes are &quot;universal.&quot; They're not just a belief system, they're an organization. They are the mage society that does the sorts of things the Diamond/Pentacle will do later- influencing Sleepers, coordinating apprenticeships, regulating access to Mysteries, etc.<br /> <br /> In the wake of Alexander's conquest, all the proto-Diamonds in the Hellenistic world meet up and start coordinating around/developing a unified dogma, forming an earlier version of the Diamond we know today, and excluding those mages who continued to focus on magic drawing on the symbols of their native cultures.<br /> <br /> I assume that after the Diamond formed, one of its chief projects was uniting all like-minded mages everywhere; &quot;The Awakened are one People&quot; is Silver Ladder doctrine for a reason. Presumably the &quot;charter members&quot; from Greece, Egypt, Persia, and India began sending emissaries to their counterparts in Rome, Gaul, China, Carthage, Nubia, Ethiopia, etc. as soon as they found out those places had mages in them. Until they were brought into the unified Diamond community (either by peaceful discussion or by hostile invasion) each of these areas would have had their own Cult, serving as the Proto-Diamond in their region. However, once the international Diamond showed up, local mages would either join the massive global network, or, if they held their local beliefs dear, they would remain Nameless.<br /> <br /> Thus, Cults would only exist until they were absorbed into the globalized blob that is the Diamond. I would think that neither Christian nor Muslim mages would ever have their own Cult; both of those religions emerged in geographic regions that ought to have been thoroughly Diamondized by the time of their inception.<br /> <br /> The Jews could have had their own small Cult before being conquered by the Babylonians; I would imagine that after that, Israelites who Awakened would face the choice of either joining the Cult of the ruling culture in order to gain access to its networks of power, or trying to develop magic drawing on their ancestral faith- a very Libertine (which is to say, Nameless at this point) inclination, as Proindrakenzol notes.<br /> <br /> However, just because Christian Vajrastras are swallowed up by the Arrow does not mean they completely abandon their religious perspective; there are two practicing Catholic mages in <i>Broken Diamond</i> that very much view the Diamond cosmology through the lens of their faith (although each does so in different ways). A mage that openly asserts that their cultural beliefs contradict and therefore invalidate Diamond doctrine is going to be Nameless until the Libertines organize, but there's plenty of room in the Orders for Sufi mystics who are officially orthodox Mystagogues, but unofficially have a very different interpretation of &quot;Magic is Alive&quot; than your average globalized mage. They may also form or modify a Legacy to crystallize their perspective into something they can pass to disciples.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to make alternate Cults, I'd agree with Proindrakenzol that you don't want to lump Christianity or Islam into a single Cult; even before the Reformation you'd have plenty of regional variation amongst Christians, and mages may more actively retain pagan symbolism than their Sleeper kin. In this kind of setting, you might want to come up with some explanation as to where the properly syncretic Diamond is, if they are anywhere; if they are non-existent, you may want to come up with a reason why neither Alexander, nor the Roman Empire, nor the Abbasid Caliphate led to the formation of the Orders. Perhaps in this alternate history, the proto-Seers managed to fully hijack the formation of the other Orders, and so the only global mage networks that have successfully formed are Ministries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T09:43:40-07:00","id":591412,"title":"","content":"Adding to what GhostTurtle posted, I think it's worth noting that you don't need a Cult to describe a magical society with a common mythology; Tome of the Mysteries first introduced the concept of Mythos, that is essentially what a Cult is, minus the actual hierarchy and organization. By the time Christianity becomes the official religion of the Roman Empire, the Orders in Europe and Levant are sufficiently organized, and any previous cults developed in the area have devolved into regional Mythoi that informed and provided with cultural context for the Orders. Cults would be relegated to isolationist kingdoms and Nameless orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:23:19-07:00","id":591781,"title":"","content":"I don't see the need to think of the Great Cults as radically seperate from Diamond culture. I see them as running into each other. I mean, even in the modern day, the Pentacle are extremely decentralised. The Great Cults are less coherent organisations and more local styles of organisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:46:29-07:00","id":1220889,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting topic -<b> How would you think about Norse Great Cult, connected to Seidr in Viking times?</b> We know the part of them are <i>Seo Hel</i>, Nordic witches dedicated to Hel that were among the most feared mages in the North. They believed their patron represented the spiritual reflection of physical decay and that the material and physical realms retain a bond with the soul upon death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:11:04-07:00","id":1220966,"title":"","content":"Worship of Odin is going to be there somewhere, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:26:16-07:00","id":1220969,"title":"","content":"I think that first would be worship of Freyja, as <a href=\"https://earthandstarryheaven.com/2017/05/17/odin-freyja/\" target=\"_blank\">she was one that taught Odin the Seidr</a>. Probably worship both of them as 'divine couple'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:33:14-07:00","id":1221002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1220969#post1220969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that first would be worship of Freyja, as <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://earthandstarryheaven.com/2017/05/17/odin-freyja/&amp;quot;]she</a> was one that taught Odin the Seidr[/URL]. Probably worship both of them as 'divine couple'.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but Odin does have more claim to the \u201cgod of magic\u201d title than Freyja does. Especially for the Awakened; him hanging himself sounds a lot like an Awakening, and him learning/creating Runes sounds a lot like discovering High Speech. We can also find all five Paths represented in Odin\u2019s image; the harbinger of death and war (Moros), the patron of berserkers and poets (Mastigos), the weaver of fate (Acanthus), the war-chief of the gods (Obrimos), and of course the master of seidr and other boundary-magics (Thyrsus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T21:43:12-07:00","id":1221068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221002#post1221002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can also find all five Paths represented in Odin\u2019s image; the harbinger of death and war (Moros), the patron of berserkers and poets (Mastigos), the weaver of fate (Acanthus), the war-chief of the gods (Obrimos), and of course the master of seidr and other boundary-magics (Thyrsus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but how this different from local Darshanas Cults? As <i>Princes of Conquered Land</i> Era pointed, you need a casts in Awakened society for each culture. So we need Norse warrior-mages, priest-mages, assassins-mages and scholar-mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:00:52-07:00","id":1221070,"title":"","content":"...Princes of the Conquered Land didn't point any such thing out. The Mutupos may mirror the Diamond Orders, but that's the Diamond Orders/Darshanas/Mutopos carry strains of thought about magic that are recurrent themes, not because of any sense mages have that society is explictly made up of those roles.<br /> <br /> I mean, you <i>can</i> do it that way, but it's not a requirement. A Convocation could just as easily be. I 'unno. Based on the archetypes of vampire covenants.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>please tell me</i> you do recognize a writing space saving trick when you see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:09:20-07:00","id":1221073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221068#post1221068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but how this different from local Darshanas Cults? As <i>Princes of Conquered Land</i> Era pointed, you need a casts in Awakened society for each culture. So we need Norse warrior-mages, priest-mages, assassins-mages and scholar-mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was only striking the broad cultural icons Norse mages could associate themselves with, not specific societies. <br /> <br /> .... Which is because, frankly, trying to find a restrictive \u201ctemplate\u201d mirroring all Darshanas, or an equally restrictive schema for all \u2018Great Cults\u2019 is going to be an exercise in futility. <br /> <br /> I mean, you\u2019ve already proven yourself willing to and capable of researching history, so you should be able to find how shamanism, witchcraft, worship etc worked in the region, and then figure out which faction would identify themselves as which Darshana/Order once they finally come into contact with their Hellenistic kin. <br /> <br /> In other words, use the bottom-up approach, not the top-down one. Don\u2019t try to fit the square peg of local culture and customs to the round hole of the Orders, and instead figure out which Order-shaped hole the square pegs can fit into. I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get something useful that way.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For example, if I were trying to figure out Awakened society in the Joseon dynasty of the Korean peninsula, I\u2019ll likely conclude that almost everyone joined the Silver Ladder and the Mysterium, with Neo-Confucianism being a big thing back then, with a minority of Buddhist- or Taoist-friendly mages joining the Arrows, without bothering to figure out precisely which social faction aligns to which Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-22-2018, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:20:46-07:00","id":1221087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221073#post1221073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, use the bottom-up approach, not the top-down one. Don\u2019t try to fit the square peg of local culture and customs to the round hole of the Orders, and instead figure out which Order-shaped hole the square pegs can fit into. I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get something useful that way.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For example, if I were trying to figure out Awakened society in the Joseon dynasty of the Korean peninsula, I\u2019ll likely conclude that almost everyone joined the Silver Ladder and the Mysterium, with Neo-Confucianism being a big thing back then, with a minority of Buddhist- or Taoist-friendly mages joining the Arrows, without bothering to figure out precisely which social faction aligns to which Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably best approach - see magical practices of particular culture, describe them - and <i>then</i> make connections with Orders when they find local groups and start to 'preach' about Atlantis. Some Orders may not have direct local reference in this process - but it will work better. Like your nice example with Korean Peninsula - there are Silver Ladder-like mages, there are some Mysterium-like mages and probably there are <b>no</b> direct Guardians-like mages. I get, don't bother with 'Atlantean model', just work with what's natural to historical part of magical traditions of local area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2018, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:46:06-07:00","id":1221092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221087#post1221087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, probably best approche - see magical practices of particular culture, describe them - and <i>then</i> make connections with Orders when they find local groups and start to 'preach' about Atlantis. Also, nice example with Korean Peninsula</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that example of mine is somewhat faulty, since the Diamond would have spread long before the Joseon dynasty rose up; it would have spread from India and the Middle East to China and then to Korea. But hey, glad you saw something useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T00:02:41-07:00","id":1221094,"title":"","content":"I think the reason folks tend to make mirrors of the orders is, from a gaming perspective, they cover the most general of social archetypes which allows for the most customization by the players and the story they want to tell. Want to be a soldier, the Guardians or Arrow provide a good home. Want to play a political character, the Silver Ladder are traditionalists and the Free Council are Libertarians. It's not perfect and we, as players, can come up with infinite variations and different spins on them, but overall Militaristic, Traditionalist, Libertine, Scholar and Investigator give us some easy homes to put our characters in. <br /> <br /> On topic, I think Seidr would be a catchall term for all mages and having the various gods representing the paths/aeons would be an interesting take on the local Norse mages. Odin as a War deity representing Moros, Freyja as the teacher of Seidr being the Obrimos deity, Loki as patron of the Mastigos path, the Norns as the representative of the Acanthus path and Baldr as the stand in for the Thrysus.<br /> <br /> Cult wise, I would see the Norse as a single cult via their shared religion/understanding of the universe, probably seeing the paths as connections to different parts of the nine realms. They could possibly be split on the subject of Ragnarok though, some believing that hastening it is better for the decaying world and others wanting to hold it back as long as possible. (You could then have Surtr being an Abyssal manifestation/entity making those supporting Ragnarok proto-Scelesti with a nihilitic philosophy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T19:44:48-07:00","id":1221355,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is going a little off-topic, but I think the most interesting use of new Great Cults is in regards to the cultures of the New World. Sure, the Diamond could have spread its paradigm beyond Afro-Eurasia through magic and the Astral Realms, but I've always preferred the idea that the mages of these areas held a variety of radically different beliefs, which might survive as part of the Free Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T21:22:33-07:00","id":1221375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221087#post1221087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...there are <b>no</b> direct Guardians-like mages. I get, don't bother with 'Atlantean model', just work with what's natural to historical part of magical traditions of local area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that too initially, but the opportunity to have Guardian-like Mages who pattern themselves after Odin's ravens Huginn and Muninn (thus fulfilling the spy archetype) is just too awesome to pass up. It doesn't have much in the way of roots in Norse society, but it's a damn cool root in Norse mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T21:26:12-07:00","id":1221377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221375#post1221375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking that too initially, but the opportunity to have Guardian-like Mages who pattern themselves after Odin's ravens Huginn and Muninn (thus fulfilling the spy archetype) is just too awesome to pass up. It doesn't have much in the way of roots in Norse society, but it's a damn cool root in Norse mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> .......yeah, okay, that's pretty damn cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T23:30:13-07:00","id":1221399,"title":"","content":"Another possibility for symbolism regarding Odin's ravens might be to connect them to the two predecessors of the Mysterium; the Pancryptiates and the Keepers of the Word. I guess the latter could be Thought, while the former could be Memory, but I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T23:57:09-07:00","id":1221401,"title":"","content":"Huginn and Muninn, aren't they thought and memory, they seem like they could easily be representative of the Mind Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T11:54:04-07:00","id":1221513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221399#post1221399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility for symbolism regarding Odin's ravens might be to connect them to the two predecessors of the Mysterium; the Pancryptiates and the Keepers of the Word.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not go with making cults related to Pancryptiates and Keepers in before mass trade contact North had in Viking Age. Remember that two millenia split over those two Orders is only effect of Greeks and Persian mages political dispute. They in the end are both hailing from Gnostikon Darshana and this Darshana is self replicating around the world. In Alexander times you got 'error' that those cults did not get along enough to become directly Mysterium in the first place, needed to wait till 12th century Byzantium and Corpus Author to become whole again. The canon proof of this is in <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> Dark Era where Gnostikon representation is one local cult, not two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-23-2018, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:13:47-07:00","id":1221518,"title":"","content":"Okay, so to hammer a bit what we collected about possible Norse Great Cult for now... Odin ( and maybe Freyja ) would be Source of Magic, becoming source for what 'Atlantists' would call Supernal Realms. <b>Hermit</b> makes great sum up of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221002#post1221002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but Odin does have more claim to the \u201cgod of magic\u201d title than Freyja does. Especially for the Awakened; him hanging himself sounds a lot like an Awakening, and him learning/creating Runes sounds a lot like discovering High Speech. We can also find all five Paths represented in Odin\u2019s image; the harbinger of death and war (Moros), the patron of berserkers and poets (Mastigos), the weaver of fate (Acanthus), the war-chief of the gods (Obrimos), and of course the master of seidr and other boundary-magics (Thyrsus).</div> </div> </div> </div>If Odin is source of Norse Awakened power, then local Nameless cults could be his 'helpers', representing 'orders' in Odinists magical duties, based on Odin's mythical companions:<br /> <br /> <b>Geri and Freki</b> - Warriors that bless with their magic berserkers on the battlefield and prepare people to Ragnarok. ( Adamntine Arrow Darshana )<br /> <br /> <b>Huginn and Muninn</b> - Mystical scouts and spies that steal secrets and guide people to their end in Lands of Dead ( Phulakeion Darshana )<br /> <br /> <b>Sleipnir</b> - Priests and law-givers that connect people with rest of Nine Realms ( Omphalos Darshana )<br /> <br /> And that's it - I do not see a real need for Gnostikon Darshana in Norse Great Cult as magic in Norse myths is <i>very</i> practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T12:32:43-07:00","id":1221523,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if all Norse mages becoming monotheistic Odin worshippers would be something I, or my players, would enjoy. With all of Norse mythology to draw on, and the ChroD lens to add over the top, everything being literally centred around Odin seems a bit boring. To add some more ChroD flavour, why not make Odin an actual Archmage, or nearly so who learned the secrets of Rune magic after his self crucifiction and who now lords over a huge court of spirits that he uses to control local mortals with his \u201cdivine\u201d powers and followers. Then to mix it up further, the Vanir of Norse myth are actually True Fae. Basically a very powerful Acanthus who has created a cult of personality around himself to assure his dominance over the world around him. Heck, Valkyries are actually a cult of Reapers who bring him the souls of the worthy dead to keep him alive well past his original lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T20:27:35-07:00","id":1221606,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was listing only one way Norse mages could build a cultural identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T21:07:14-07:00","id":1221611,"title":"","content":"Still, according to sources, Odin worship was (almost) universal in the North. Not all worshiped him as personal god, but he was acknowledge as God of Magic, Wisdom and War. And, well, other Great Cults we have in Dark Eras books are also pointing to the widest, but still singular interpretation of particular magical tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:50:00-07:00","id":1221669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions?p=1221611#post1221611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, according to sources, Odin worship was (almost) universal in the North. Not all worshiped him as personal god, but he was acknowledge as God of Magic, Wisdom and War. And, well, other Great Cults we have in Dark Eras books are also pointing to the widest, but still singular interpretation of particular magical tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody devoted themselves to a single god the way that the initiates did in the Graeco-Roman mystery cults. There were no priests or temple keepers that only visited a specific god's temple. Remember, getting the attention of a god was not considered a good thing, hence why people used kennings, titles and bynames for the gods rather than their real names. The real names of Frey and Freya are literally forgotten because people didn't use them.<br /> The Allfather would likely be venerated more often due to mages having more cultural events tied to magic, but that's about it unless you want to depart from what's known about the Norse religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}